# Incremental Code Modification Principles

> file_patterns: ["*.py", "*.md", "*.json", "*.yaml"]
> description: Guidelines for making progressive code changes

## Step by Step Approach
Make changes incrementally and verify each step:
- Modify one critical point at a time
- Verify effect after each modification
- Maintain stability of other components

## Modification Strategy
Strategic approach to code changes:
- Progress from abstract to concrete
- Move from general to specific
- Prefer augmentation over replacement

## Verification Process
Ensure quality of changes:
- Run tests after each change
- Compare behavior before and after changes
- Confirm no unintended side effects

## Best Practices
Guidelines for implementing changes:
- Find appropriate location within existing structure
- Maintain consistent abstraction levels
- Ensure new content matches context expression style

## Common Pitfalls
Mistakes to avoid:
- Avoid changing too many things at once
- Don't alter existing abstraction levels
- Always verify effects of changes

## Code Review Process
- Review changes in small batches
- Focus on one component at a time
- Ensure changes follow project standards
- Verify documentation is updated

## Testing Requirements
- Write tests before making changes
- Update existing tests as needed
- Verify all tests pass after changes
- Document test modifications

## Documentation Updates
- Update relevant documentation
- Document change rationale
- Note any breaking changes
- Keep changelog current

## Validation Requirements
- Changes must be atomic and verifiable
- Each change must maintain system stability
- Changes should follow existing patterns
- All changes must be tested 